The suite runs in that copy with cwd = the copy and PYTHONPATH = the copy only, so the mutated modules are the ones
imported. The test module itself refuses to run if dltrain resolves outside its own tree (P8SEG-IMPORT-GUARD); a
mutant whose output shows that guard is a HARNESS ERROR, never a detection. Every mutation must match its source text
exactly once.

A mutant counts as DETECTED when a test that passes in the unmutated baseline copy fails or errors. Tests listed in
--exclude (known baseline failures) are dropped before the run, and the run stops at the first failure (failfast).
Mutants marked "layer" disable one layer of a multi-layer guard: they may survive by design, and their combined
mutant must be detected.

Nothing is deleted. Run inside the lane slice:
  RUN/tmp/p2fix3/py.sh RUN/tmp/p8-segment-tests/p8_segment_mutants.py [--jobs 3] [--exclude TEST_ID ...] [NAME ...]
